ndation Lifetime Achievement Award, the National Book Award, and a MacArthur Fellowship.\\n\\n2007-2008: Ana Castillo\\n\\nChicana novelist Ana Castillo read from her novel The Guardians on ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.grinnell.edu/campus-life/arts-culture/writersgrinnell/distinguished-authors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d67\"},\"ref\":\"d67\",\"snippet\":\" ... Norton & Company, 2007. H. L. Mitchell Award (2008); Liberty Legacy Foundation Award (2008); Robert F. Kennedy Book Award (2008); International Labor History Association Book of the Year Award (2009) »\\n\\nHoogenboom, Hilde (NHC Fellow, 2000–01), trans. The Memoirs of Catherine the Great. Translated by Hilde Hoogenboom and Mark ... \",\"title\":\"https://nationalhumanitiescenter.org/scholarly-programs/books-by-fellows/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d68\"},\"ref\":\"d68\",\"snippet\":\" ... with the Dragon Tattoo (first English translation, 2008), Keith Gessen, All the Sad Young Literary Men (2008), Steven Millhauser, Dangerous Laughter (2008), Joseph O'Neill, Netherland (2008), Richard Price, Lush Life (2008), John Updike, The Widows of Eastwick (2008), Curtis Sittenfeld, Prep (2005), Hilary Mantel, Wolf Hall (2009)\",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/a-century-of-reading-the-10-books-that-defined-the-2000s/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d69\"},\"ref\":\"d69\",\"snippet\":\" ... Makobe | Nkune se, Mphe se! | Sepedi | |\\n| 2009 | J.J. Ncongwane | Tikhatsi Letimatima | Swati | |\\n| 2008 | No award | No award | No award | |\\n| 2007 | Otty E.H.M Nxumalo | Body of work | Zulu | |\\n\\nNovel Award\\n\\n**Table 3**: Novel Award Winners\\n\\n| Year | W